# Architecture Guard Rails

Phase: **v0.3 stabilization**.

## Stack (do not substitute)

| Component | Is | Is NOT |
|---|---|---|
| Object store | RustFS | MinIO (test-only fallback) |
| Catalog | Lakekeeper (Iceberg REST) | Nessie |
| Object-store data I/O | OpenDAL | raw `aws-sdk-s3`, ad hoc S3 clients |
| Query engine | DataFusion | DuckDB, Polars |
| Catalog DB | Postgres | SQLite |
| Local orchestration | Docker Compose | Kubernetes, bare `docker run` as docs default |
| SQL queries | DataFusion (over Iceberg) | Direct Postgres queries |

## Hard Stops

- Do not reintroduce Nessie or MinIO as active defaults.
- Do not present planned features as implemented.
- Do not bypass OpenDAL for object-store reads, writes, list, head, or delete.
- Do not add JVM dependencies.
- Do not add Kubernetes guidance for v0.3.

## Allowed Integration Boundaries

Direct HTTP is allowed only for explicit integration boundaries:

- Lakekeeper catalog bootstrap and project/warehouse setup.
- Health checks and doctor/preflight checks.
- Signed setup calls where a crate boundary does not expose the needed operation.

Keep these calls narrow, documented, fallible, and covered by tests when touched.

## Data Correctness

- Catalog/store consistency is a correctness requirement.
- Ingest must not report full success if object upload succeeds but Iceberg
  metadata commit fails.
- Re-running unchanged ingest/query flows should be deterministic or document
  the known limitation.
- Placeholder workflows must not return success semantics once their behavior is
  touched.

## Delivery Boundary

Container, Compose, CI, release, and deployment documentation rules live in
`.cursor/rules/docker-ci-standards`. Do not duplicate those rules here.
